# Compact Policy

Compact only at major workflow boundaries after durable project context is written.

## Source Of Truth

- `AGENTS.md`
- `.planning/STATE.md`
- `.planning/phases/`
- `.planning/checkpoints/`
- `openspec/`
- git diff and log

## Instruction

When a checkpoint reports `compact_status: pending`, compact is recommended for
context hygiene and recoverability. Prefer `/compact` at a stable boundary, but
do not interrupt otherwise-continuable work solely to ask for manual compact
when automatic compaction/recovery is available and repository checkpoint files
are durable. When a checkpoint reports `compact_status: not_needed`, the task is
at a stopping point and state is already updated; compact is optional before
starting a new thread or using the checkpoint as handoff context.

When an external API or harness runs compaction for a pending gate, record the returned payload with `record_compact_result.py`.
The compact record is evidence for the gate; repository files remain the source of truth.
